        "summary": "New section after 2.8, modeled on 2.5b: reached only when every gate above is satisfied and the planned action is merge - one execution per merge attempt, not per patience tick. The command string is passed to bash -c verbatim (never built from PR-derived text) with FLOW_HEAD_SHA/BASE_REF/PR_NUMBER/SPEC_ID as environment; one blocking foreground call at the host tool's 600s bound (the orchestrator follow-up replaced the worker's `timeout` binary, which is not stock on macOS and would have refused every valid command with 127). Exit 0 = green; any non-zero = NEEDS_HUMAN with exit code + last stderr line (BLOCKED stays reserved for server-side refusals); missing/unexecutable/timeout/signal all block, never skip. The wrong-tree warning states the command runs on the base checkout and must key on $FLOW_HEAD_SHA. --dry-run reports would-run. Phase 0 reads the key off the existing lcfg capture (prose-diet pins one config get); Phase 4 evidence gains mergeVerdict.",
